  "headline": "1+1d single-step growth on a ring (L=4096, 64 rings, 8,000 sweeps): β=0.3119 against the exact KPZ 1/3, with α=0.4875 from saturation (exact 1/2) giving z=α/β=1.563 (exact 3/2) and 1/z=0.640 (exact 2/3). Same pipeline on the controls: Edwards–Wilkinson β=0.2424 (exact 1/4) and random deposition β=0.4988 (exact 1/2, and its w²(t) tracks the closed form p(1−p)t to 0.9%) — three separated classes, so the 1/3 is a measurement and not an artifact of the fit. Height fluctuations are skewed -0.1789 (droplet) and -0.2702 (flat) against the λ<0-mirrored Tracy–Widom predictions -0.2241 (GUE) and -0.2935 (GOE): each geometry lands nearer its own law (2.5× and 2.0×). · 290s",
